$\begin{align}
h'(x)&=\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[ \dfrac{e^{2x}}{x-3} \right]
\\\\
&=\dfrac{(x-3)\cdot \dfrac{d}{dx}[e^{2x}]-e^{2x}\cdot \dfrac{d}{dx}[x-3]}{(x-3)^2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{(x-3)\cdot 2e^{2x}-e^{2x}\cdot 1}{(x-3)^2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{e^{2x}(2x-7)}{(x-3)^2}
\end{align}$

Now let's look for $x$-values where $h'$ is zero or undefined.
